rom the get-go steel  ball bran I was expecting him to be a  much more profound presence especially  with His infinite luck and his really  fun stand instead we end the series with  him winning the race which is fantastic  I do love the end result but Poco Loco  feels like quite possibly the only  character who was never properly  explored and flushed out now as for the  steel ball run itself I should also say  that this is by far my favorite setting  for a Jojo series from the moment I  found out about it in chapter 1 I was  fully on board because it's so easy to  get invested into a story with an  overarching contest even if that does  eventually get pushed into the  background in favor of searching for a  corpse now actively though it makes an  author's job so much easier  because there is always a prime driving  factor for characters to be moving and  committing the actions that they do so  in steel ball run I never felt like I  was questioning the purpose of the story  as I did come to in part 6 for example  and as much as this may pain me because  I love diamond is unbreakable  steel bull run is probably my favorite  part thus far everything about it is  just so solid it has a brilliant setting  characters containing a lot of depth  interesting stands that don't outshine  their users and - typically bittersweet  Jojo ending where the kid who gyro was  ultimately doing all of this to save  caught a cold and just went and died  anyway which is so tragic that I  couldn't even do anything but laugh at  that point after everything that had  happened fate just went and did its  thing anyway but now it's time to move  on to the last stage of the journey I  guess  Jojo Leon Jojo Lyon Jojo Leon a series  that is still ongoing but we're going to  consume and review it anyway  actually don't know how many chapters  there are but I think it's a substantial  chunk because people have said that it's  been in publication since for 2011 so  even on a monthly basis and  incorporating breaks that is still an  ass-ton of content in 2020 surely and  people have also started asking me about  whether or not I'll continue to talk  about Jojo after I finished a series  like I've had more than a few requests  to start passed an encyclopedia modeled  after the devil for encyclopedia that I  do on my one-piece channel and to be  perfectly honest that is something that  I would love to do however what I don't  know at this stage you should I be doing  on this channel or his JoJo's Bizarre  Adventure such a mega property that it  would need its own channel old questions  that are currently spinning through my  head but that pretty much does it for  this review of the Magnificent steel  ball run if you enjoyed this video and  the content this channel produced in  general then please do consider donating  to the new worldview patreon because the  support of all for your amazing people  is what continues to make this channel  possible and if patreon isn't quite your  style then please do leave this video a  like share or subscribe because it also  helps support this channel and  incredible amount and if you'd like to  join the fun at any time then please do  head over to my discord server where a  wide array of Shannara takes place on a  daily basis and finally please do  comment with your thoughts on steel ball  run this has been the new world review  and I'll see you next time

